{#def attachment, alt=None, caption=None #}

{#
Default renderer for an `attachment` node inside a Rich Text Document.

The framework hands us the resolved `Attachment` row plus the per-embed
`alt` and `caption` text from the AST. We dispatch on content type:

- Images: render as `<figure>` with a resized variant (max 1600x1600).
  Edit the `attachment.variant(...)` call to taste - different limits,
  different formats, lightbox wrappers, lazy-loading attributes, etc.
- PDFs: a labelled link that opens in a new tab.
- Anything else: a plain download link.

Edit this file freely. The renderer only knows it should
route every `attachment` node through here, the visual layout is yours.
#}

{% if attachment.content_type.startswith("image/") %}
  {% set variant = attachment.variant(resize_to_fit=(1600, 1600, {"size": "down"})) %}
  <figure class="rich-text-image">
    <img src="{{ variant.url }}"
         alt="{{ alt or '' }}"
         loading="lazy">
    {% if caption %}<figcaption>{{ caption }}</figcaption>{% endif %}
  </figure>
{% elif attachment.content_type == "application/pdf" %}
  <a href="{{ attachment.url }}"
     class="rich-text-pdf"
     target="_blank"
     rel="noopener">
    {{ attachment.filename }}
  </a>
{% else %}
  <a href="{{ attachment.url }}"
     class="rich-text-file"
     download>
    {{ attachment.filename }}
  </a>
{% endif %}
